Maven Web Application using Eclipse
Step 1: Open Eclipse
1. Open Eclipse IDE.
2. Select your workspace.
3. Click Launch.
Step 2: Create Maven Project
1. Click File → New → Other.
2. Expand Maven.
3. Select Maven Project.
4. Click Next.
5. Tick Create a simple project (skip archetype selection).
6. Click Next.
Enter these details:
Field	Value
Group Id	com.example
Artifact Id	MavenWeb
Version	1.0
Packaging	war


Click Finish.
Step 3: Configure pom.xml
Open pom.xml.

Replace its contents with:
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0
         https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">

    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>MavenWeb</artifactId>
    <version>1.0</version>

    <packaging>war</packaging>

</project>

Save using Ctrl + S.
Step 4: Create HTML file
1. Right-click the project.
2. Select New → Folder.
3. Name it src/main/webapp.
If src/main already exists, create only the webapp folder inside it.
4. Right-click webapp.
5. Select New → HTML File.
6. Name it index.html.
Paste:
<html>
<body>
    <h1>Hello Maven Web Application!</h1>
    <p>My first Maven Web Project.</p>
</body>
</html>

Save it.
Step 5: Build the project
1. Right-click MavenWeb.
2. Select Run As → Maven build...
3. In Goals, enter:
clean package

4. Click Run.
Wait for:
BUILD SUCCESS

Step 6: Deploy using Tomcat
You need Apache Tomcat configured in Eclipse.
1. Open the Servers tab.
2. Right-click → New → Server.
3. Select Apache → Tomcat v10.1 Server.
4. Select your extracted Tomcat installation directory.
5. Click Finish.
6. Right-click the server → Add and Remove.
7. Add MavenWeb.
8. Click Finish.
9. Right-click the server → Start.
Step 7: View final output
Open your browser:
http://localhost:8080/MavenWeb/

Expected output:

Hello Maven Web Application!